# A/B (round 1.3.9): lwIP sends SACK options (RFC 2018). Negotiated in the
# SYN, so on every TCP conn (control and DERP). With lwIP's 4-segment
# receive window a segment lost from a flight seldom draws the three
# duplicate ACKs of a fast retransmit, and a server that is not told
# SACK has neither the tail-loss probe nor RACK (Linux runs both only on
# SACK conns): what is left is its RTO, srtt + ≥ 200 ms, doubling per
# repeat — 1.3.8's 2.0–6.2-s netmap tails, if they are losses
# (`map body:` stalls). With SACK the hole is resent after ~1 RTT. Costs
# 32 B per TCP pcb (4 SACK ranges, LWIP_TCP_MAX_SACK_NUM) and lwIP's SACK
# code (flash; LWIP_IRAM_OPTIMIZATION is off); no buffer — the blocks
# describe the out-of-order segments lwIP keeps anyway (OOSEQ ≤ 4).
CONFIG_LWIP_TCP_SACK_OUT=y
